                <pb facs="1131" n="1071" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg1071"/>

                <head>Mr. Sullivan to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bogota,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 18, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    correspondence (A and B) had between the Colombian government and myself, on the
                    request of the Spanish minister at Washington, invoking our friendly aid (per
                    your dispatch No. 39 of April 14th last) not to let the war steamer Cuyler go to
                    sea during the existing war between Spain and certain South American republics.
                    I think the answer is satisfactory.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PETER J. SULLIVAN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d658-a1.xml" xpointer="d658-a1"/>
